From: =?UTF-8?q?C=C3=BCneyt=20=C4=B0nan?= <cuneytinan37@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 02:55:35 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] autoDraw: also when pawns, kings and bishops lock both
 sides out

A position where neither side can ever be mated is dead (FIDE 5.2.2) and
the game ends at once; scalachess draws it today when the material is
insufficient. Ask Mateless's lock detector too, for both sides: pawns,
kings and bishops that no series of legal moves can open. It is asked
after a capture or a pawn move and one move later (halfmove clock 0 or
1): a lock can appear only then, at once, or once an en passant right
has lapsed or a king has stepped out of a pawn's check. Before its fixed
point it fails at once with a knight, rook or queen on the board, two
bishops of one side on squares of one colour, or an en passant square.
Standard and From Position only.

Of 195,287 Lichess games up to September 2026 lost on time though the
flagged side could never be mated (chasolver's data to July, a scan of
Lichess's databases for August and September), scalachess draws 138,572
today; with this 190,465, the 51,893 more as dead positions before the
flag fell. In August and September 8,718 drawn games went on for a
median of 14 plies after such a lock had appeared. autoDraw costs about
5-7 ns more per move in game positions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018qH7RHdrNYQtzmaq7gfmhu
---
 core/src/main/scala/Position.scala | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/src/main/scala/Position.scala b/core/src/main/scala/Position.scala
index f029ae1c..efc365d6 100644
--- a/core/src/main/scala/Position.scala
+++ b/core/src/main/scala/Position.scala
@@ -83,7 +83,16 @@ case class Position(board: Board, history: History, variant: Variant, color: Col
 
   inline def staleMate: Boolean = variant.staleMate(this)
 
-  inline def autoDraw: Boolean = variant.autoDraw(this) || variant.specialDraw(this)
+  inline def autoDraw: Boolean = variant.autoDraw(this) || variant.specialDraw(this) || lockedOut
+
+  /** A dead position (FIDE 5.2.2): pawns, kings and bishops that no series of legal moves can open, so
+    * neither side can ever be mated (chess.mateless.Lock). Asked after a capture or a pawn move and one
+    * move later (halfmove clock 0 or 1): a lock appears only then, at once, or once an en passant right
+    * has lapsed or a king has stepped out of a pawn's check. Standard and From Position only.
+    */
+  def lockedOut: Boolean =
+    history.halfMoveClock.value < 2 && (variant.standard || variant.fromPosition) &&
+      mateless.Lock.cannotBeMated(this, Color.White) && mateless.Lock.cannotBeMated(this, Color.Black)
 
   def opponentHasInsufficientMaterial: Boolean =
     variant.opponentHasInsufficientMaterial(this) ||
